From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:09:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Release build with ccache and a slim runtime image; panel
 keeps the compile cache

- Dockerfile: Release instead of Debug; ccache in a BuildKit cache mount so
  rebuilds only recompile changed files; build dir removed in the same layer;
  runtime stage on debian:12-slim with only the server, its non-libc shared
  libraries (gathered with ldd) and the tools the start scripts use; files
  chowned on COPY instead of a duplicating chown layer; .git no longer copied
  (the commit hash define forced full recompiles).
- .dockerignore: drop .git.
- Control panel: builder prune keeps exec.cachemount records; after a rebuild
  only records unused for 72h are pruned; Free up space prunes the rest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GZgkReFMTa8JWavQEivVUA
